prs.body:
Canonical integration branch for SWAP5. PR remains draft and is not approved for merge to main.

Completed/qualified integration through F-CI13, with admission status kept explicit per work unit.

- F-CI02 exact canonical reference root / B1.10 provenance;
- F-CI03 transaction core + worker-owned solver scratch;
- F-CI04 canonical state/forcing/config/result contracts + externally atomic generic runtime;
- F-CI05 exact B1.10 physical preimage;
- F-CI06 controlled B1.10 source port + water checkpoint;
- F-CI07 worker-local legacy trial rollback capsule;
- F-CI08 physical/process continuation state + attempt-context rollback;
- F-CI09 canonical B1.10 transaction-model binding substrate;
- F-CI10 worker/job-local unrounded trial-mass contract + qualified-profile storage/mass seam;
- F-CI11 controlled legacy interval/mass source port with generic physical interval boundaries independent of calendar day boundaries;
- F-CI12 executable physical-advance binding plus unit-explicit temporal-difference characterization;
- F-CI13 explicit physical-trial status contract and recoverable terminal Richards nonconvergence mapping for the canonical worker path.

B1.10 remains the physical oracle: 63 sources, 1,863,575 bytes, manifest `2dfc004f1bae3fc249f384d4f947a07ed4627e83e251ce6557d03092f0b4d1b1`.

F-CI13 source head `538d51df4be3780a5bb092767304749dfc800899` passed canonical workflow run `34104845258`; job `101687946143` reported `FCI13_GATE_PASS` with GNU Fortran 13.3.0. The complete sequential F-CI03 -> F-CI13 chain passed on that source head.

F-CI13 preserves existing internal timestep retries and the existing TRIDAG alternative-solver route. Only persistent Richards nonconvergence at minimum timestep is classified as `RETRYABLE_NUMERICAL` for the canonical worker path; its trial state is restored and unrounded trial mass invalidated before postprocessing. Standalone legacy behavior remains unchanged. Invalid/configuration `swap_error` paths remain fatal and are not retried.

Qualification boundary: the exact B1.10 HeadCalc terminal branch and the F-CI13 successor postimage are source-pinned, while executable failure semantics are tested O0/O2 with a deterministic legacy testdouble. A real Hupsel/B1.10 case has not yet been deliberately forced into terminal minimum-dt nonconvergence.

Still explicitly NOT admitted: production B1.10 `execute_reference_interval`, qualified scalar temporal-error acceptance policy, complete optional-process temporal characterization, complete snow/macropore storage/failure qualification, reentrant/parallel legacy backend qualification, and B2 reference admission.

No physical formula, constitutive relation, Jacobian formula, convergence tolerance, retry scaling policy, mass tolerance or calendar-event rule is changed by F-CI13.

Central-regie recomposition of the already qualified MC-IRR01 owner on current canonical `c7879cdf54fce43d668877f5a0a4d71806df7426`.

Admission scope:
- fixed sprinkling and scheduled surface event routing;
- frequency, daily-rate and rate-cap policies;
- sensor/SSDI authoritative mass path;
- management retry/restart and nonfinite fail-closed guards.

Reconciliation:
- all production and test blobs are byte-identical to qualified integration head `4ed0a6d62eae82f46d9f79d06b764e141474c9e2`;
- prior owner qualification run 37768355395 and isolated integration run 37774945522 succeeded at O0/O2;
- none of the candidate's changed paths changed on canonical since the qualified base;
- Rutter interception, dynamic-top boundary, and irrigation transaction/restart dependencies show no canonical drift;
- no new production physics was developed by regie.

The PR intentionally triggers the existing F-APP07 owner workflow once for the current persisted admission postimage. No duplicate manual dispatch is requested. Canonical admission remains bounded to the qualified capability list and does not imply unrestricted irrigation coverage or global CI green.
